      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think this is fine. It\u0027s the same idiom used by runtime-shader, when sampling a child shader - evaluate the new local coords, then overwrite the provider so that children see the remaining matrix as the identity. I don\u0027t think our current architecture has a better option - this is the only thing that prevents children from accidentally baking in this node\u0027s local matrix.",
